# Docs first + same-turn sync

**Prefer docs** for orientation, how-to-run, intended rules, handoffs. Session start: see `session-independence.mdc` (AGENTS + HANDOFF + matching rules; cross-app PROJECT_STATE / ARCHITECTURE). Do not open large code trees to “learn” the app.

**Open code only when needed:** implement/fix; verify exists/unused/`shared/` consumers; run the app’s existing test/self-check before “fixed”. Prefer the smallest file that proves the claim. Truth axes: `session-independence.mdc`. Layers/limits: `architecture.mdc`.

**Same-turn sync (keep docs current):** if this turn changes behaviour, entrypoints, handoffs, dry-run/`--run`, or not-built status → update the owner doc **before** saying done:
- app how-to-run / built state → that app’s `docs/HANDOFF.md` (`AGENTS.md` only if a handbook claim changed)
- cross-app handoff / built vs not-built → `docs/PROJECT_STATE.md`
- locks → owner in `docs/DECISIONS.md`

**No doc fiction:** never write built/not-built/column shapes from memory — verify in code, then write the doc.

**Stale doc while working:** flag FACT inconsistency (doc path + code path). Docs-only and code clearly right → fix the doc same turn. Grouping / matching / approval / live writes → stop and ask.
